panvk: render pass / image trace for profiling (debug only, not packaged)

While /tmp/pvtrace exists, every closed JM batch logs to /tmp/pvtrace.log:
caller offset in libvulkan_panfrost.so, job count, framebuffer size,
tile size, first / spilled batch, and per attachment format / modifier
(AFBC, UINT, LIN) / load op (- none, C clear, L load, ! always) / store.
While /tmp/pvtrace-img exists, every image creation logs format, extent,
usage, flags and the chosen modifier. /tmp is shared with Steam's
pressure-vessel containers, so it works for Proton games.
Apply on top of the series: git apply mainline/mesa-g77/debug/pvtrace.patch

